{"id": "EUVD-2026-87843", "enisaUuid": "27e5c1bf-42ff-321d-b90f-a489088b4e49", "description": "MONAI before 1.6.0 contains an unsafe deserialization vulnerability in the NumpyReader class that unconditionally uses numpy.load with allow_pickle=True when loading .npy and .npz files. Attackers can craft malicious .npy files with pickle payloads that execute arbitrary code when loaded through MONAI's standard data pipeline.", "datePublished": "2026-09-27T01:28:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-28T13:56:50", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI/security/advisories/GHSA-wg9g-w2j2-8pgr", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/monai-before-1.6.0-remote-code-execution-via-numpyreader"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-100845", "GHSA-4jj3-3266-2688", "PYSEC-2026-4020"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1356a63f-4f84-3114-b23b-dde09b1fb468", "product": {"name": "MONAI", "vendor": {"name": "Project-MONAI"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "055c5a24-dca0-3bd4-8ef9-f403c68ac057", "vendor": {"name": "Project-MONAI"}}], "isExploited": false}